● The file identity_service/login_localhost_3000_problem.md already documents this exact issue and its fix. Here's the explanation:
     
  Root Cause

  When you click "Sign in" at http://login.cloudweave.xyz:3000/login, the identity service container builds the Dex authorize URL that your browser navigates to. That container was running with:

  PUBLIC_HOSTNAME=localhost
  DEX_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000/dex
  DEX_PORTAL_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/callback

  So every authorize URL it built pointed to localhost:3000/dex/auth?... instead of login.cloudweave.xyz:3000/dex/auth?....

  Why localhost? The identity_service/docker-compose.yml uses ${PUBLIC_HOSTNAME:-localhost} — when there's no .env file setting PUBLIC_HOSTNAME, Docker Compose defaults it to localhost.

  The Fix (already applied in the doc)

  Two things were changed:

  1. Created identity_service/.env with:
  PUBLIC_HOSTNAME=login.cloudweave.xyz
  1. This overrides the Docker Compose default.
  2. Updated dex/generated/dex.env — changed DEX_PORTAL_REDIRECT_URI from localhost:3000 to login.cloudweave.xyz:3000.

  Then the identity service container was recreated, and after restart it correctly builds:
  authorizeUrl: http://login.cloudweave.xyz:3000/dex/auth?...

  One remaining issue in Dex config

  The Dex static client config (dex/config.yaml:73) still hardcodes the redirect URI as localhost:3000:

  - id: libcloud-portal
    name: libcloud Role Portal
    secret: fsuvOH7yZEoe8fjyP3j957_D8XpLxRFFx9dUM-ZHr80
    redirectURIs:
      - http://localhost:3000/auth/callback    # ← needs login.cloudweave.xyz

  Even with the identity service fix, Dex will reject the OAuth callback because http://login.cloudweave.xyz:3000/auth/callback doesn't match the registered redirect URI of
  http://localhost:3000/auth/callback. You may need to add the production redirect URI there too (or replace it if the portal runs exclusively at login.cloudweave.xyz).

